---
description: Closed option lists on models are enum, not constants
alwaysApply: true
---

# Enum for options

A fixed set of string choices on a model is `enum`, not a frozen `%w` constant plus `inclusion`. Status, role, priority, and category already follow this. Do not add `CATEGORIES`, `STATUSES`, or `ROLES`.

```ruby
# bad
CATEGORIES = %w[pricing refunds billing].freeze
validates :category, presence: true, inclusion: { in: CATEGORIES }
```

```ruby
# good
enum :category, { pricing: "pricing", refunds: "refunds", billing: "billing" }, validate: true
```

Do not put a SQL `default:` on that column unless it is boolean.
